Reliability metrics help organizations measure how consistently Azure services deliver expected performance and availability.

Common reliability metrics include:

* Service uptime
* Mean Time Between Failures (MTBF)
* Mean Time To Recover (MTTR)
* Incident frequency
* Availability percentage
* Recovery success rate

# Real-Life Example:
For example, an organization may establish a target of 99.95% application availability while continuously measuring service performance against this objective.

# Real-Life Use Case:
A real-life use case is executive management reviewing monthly reliability reports to evaluate operational performance.

Reliability metrics enable objective assessment and continuous service improvement.
